    "narrative": "The offensive engine for Ghost Ride the WHIP centers on a high-upside trio today, led by **James Wood** (76.14). Facing a favorable matchup against Mike Burrows (4.71 xERA), **James Wood**\u2019s elite .425 xwOBA paired with an order-leading role makes him the day's primary target for production. **Corbin Carroll** (72.02) remains a critical cornerstone against Walker Buehler; while the park factor is slightly negative, **Corbin Carroll**\u2019s dynamic platoon advantage and current form make him an essential start. We are also leaning heavily into **Isaac Paredes** (68.21), whose matchup against Miles Mikolas is statistically our strongest; the combination of a high SP xERA (4.59) and the positive park factor provides an excellent floor for someone batting in the heart of the order.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved balancing the depth at the UTIL spot, where **Kyle Karros** (60.11) narrowly edged out other options. His surge is driven by a massive +19% boost from the matchup against Eric Lauer, whose struggles provide a significant lift to our bench utility players. Conversely, we are keeping a close eye on **Brice Turang** (57.67); while his speed is vital to our stolen base requirements, the matchup against Dustin May is stifling his upside, and the 55% stolen base prevention rate of the battery serves as a cautionary flag for his aggressiveness on the paths.\n\nRegarding risks, we are operating with \"Lineup Pending\" status across the board, which introduces variance for players like **Gabriel Moreno** and **Dalton Rushing**. **Dalton Rushing** in particular sits at a thin 42.48 score due to the platoon disadvantage against Kyle Freeland, which is only slightly mitigated by the pitcher's xERA. We continue to monitor the status of **Trevor Story** and **Giancarlo Stanton**, who remain sidelined on the IL, while keeping **Josh Naylor** and **Seiya Suzuki** ready for their return to the active rotation. With other prospects like **Travis Bazzana**, **Edwin Arroyo**, **Cole Young**, and **Henry Bolte** waiting in the wings, along with **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Max Muncy**, and **Zach McKinstry**, we are well-positioned to pivot should any late-breaking weather or lineup changes compromise our starters.",
